Registration back-off for a REGISTER that could not be sent, issue #77,
docs/sip.md.

libre retries a REGISTER that was sent and failed (no answer, an error
response) after 30 to 60 s, doubling to 15 to 30 min (RFC 5626 section
4.5), and starts again from the top on success. One that could not be sent
at all (no network yet, no transport) was not retried by anyone. Now it is
given the same back-off; unregistering still returns the error.

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

diff -u a/src/sipreg/reg.c b/src/sipreg/reg.c
--- a/src/sipreg/reg.c
+++ b/src/sipreg/reg.c
@@ -413,10 +413,23 @@
 
 int sipreg_send(struct sipreg *reg)
 {
+	int err;
+
 	if (!reg)
 		return EINVAL;
 
-	return request(reg, true);
+	err = request(reg, true);
+
+	/* A REGISTER that could not be sent (no network, no transport) is
+	 * retried with the same back-off as one that failed, instead of not
+	 * at all. Unregistering (expires 0) still returns the error. */
+	if (err && reg->expires) {
+		tmr_start(&reg->tmr, failwait(++reg->failc), tmr_handler, reg);
+		reg->resph(err, NULL, reg->arg);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	return err;
 }
 
 
